{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqfkg7qyrwv","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"FeatureBench KB build cost per repo sonnet onboarding orchestration tokens and validation wall clock for payoff analysis","summary":"Measured cost to build the ON-self-learning KB per project repo, sonnet learner, FAILED/retry rounds EXCLUDED (2026-06-15). This is the denominator for the 'does KB pay off' calc vs eval-time token savings. Per repo (worker ORCHESTRATION tokens = the Claude Code agent running the shell steps; validation wall-clock = the nested learner pass): pandas 62.9k tok / 420s / 20 kept / 15 exported; astropy 47.6k / 471s / 20 / 19; sphinx 51.3k / 446s / 20 / 19; sympy 49.2k / 559s / 20 / 15; seaborn ~22k (bundled in the opus+sonnet compare run, 44.7k total for both) / 448s / 21 / 16. Five-repo orchestration total ~233k tokens, AVG ~47k tokens + ~8min learner wall-clock per repo. CRITICAL CAVEAT: the nested learner (onboard-learn.js spawns a headless `claude -p` validating up to 500 mined candidates with source read-access) does NOT log its token usage — onboard-learn-report.json has kept/rejected only. So ~47k/repo is a LOWER BOUND on true build cost; the dominant learning compute (the claude -p validation pass, ~7-9min/repo) is uncaptured and must be instrumented in onboard-learn.js for an exact figure. Each repo's KB is an isolated per-workspace store (15-19 notes exported per repo at --k 100 --min-score 0). Excludes ~255k tokens burned on the pre-stabilization failed rounds (gate/timeout bugs) and ~225k on FeatureBench setup+manifest. For payoff: compare ~47k+ build cost/repo against (per-task eval token delta when KB present) x (tasks per repo); FeatureBench pilot has 3 instances/repo so KB must save >~15k tokens/task to break even on orchestration alone — likely needs the resolve-rate lift (not just token savings) to justify.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T18:48:12.346Z","vec":[-0.06595949083566666,0.016173485666513443,-0.0476864129